  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar HCFC Phase Out Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2nd Tranche - -MYA/PHA/80/INV/19 With UN Environment, as the lead implementing agency, submitted to the 68th Meeting of the Executive Committee for the stage I of the HCFC phase-out management plan (HPMP). The Government is proposing to follow the Montreal Protocol schedule and adopt a staged approach to achieve a 35% reduction by 2020, complete phase-out by 2030 and a service tail to 2040. The reduction of controlled use of the ozone-depleting substances (ODS) set out in Appendix 1-A (#The Substances#) to a sustained level of 2.80 ODP tonnes prior to 1 January 2020 in compliance with Montreal Protocol schedules.</narrative>
  </description>
